<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S GIANT SLALOM WINNER.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S GIANT SLALOM WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>VAIL, Colorado 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a brief</p>
<p>profile of the winner of the World Cup Finals men's giant</p>
<p>slalom race on Saturday:</p>
<p>Name: Michael von Gruenigen</p>
<p>Age: 27</p>
<p>Nationality: Swiss</p>
<p>World Cup wins: 11 -- all giant slaloms.</p>
<p>This season - 4 victories: Alta Badia, Kranjska Gora, Shiga</p>
<p>Kogen, World Cup Finals-Vail</p>
<p>Other feats: Won his second successive World Cup giant slalom</p>
<p>title this season. Won giant slalom world championship at</p>
<p>Sestriere. Captured world championship bronze in both slalom</p>
<p>and giant slalom at 1996 world championships.</p>
</text>
